{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib disproof of Farideh Firoozbakht's 2015 conjecture on OEIS A086766 (`OeisA86766.conjecture2` in google-deepmind/formal-conjectures), which asserted that for every positive integer n not of the form 10^m there exists r >= 1 such that the r-fold decimal concatenation of n followed by the digit 1 is prime. We exhibit two explicit 6-digit counterexamples, n = 104040 and n = 750760, proving via algebraic difference-of-squares factorizations that every candidate is composite for all r >= 1.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Maxence Faldor"
    }
  ],
